// design-system.jsonc: the design system and agentic composition: its decisions and the requirements its models are held to (an area part: items whose id is ds- and a number, or starts d-ds-; docs/design-system.md).
// A part of the Strata specification; spec.jsonc lists the parts. Generated by scripts/split-spec.mjs
// the first time, edited in place after that. See specifications/README.md.
{
  "decisions": [
    {"id":"d-ds-1","ref":"D-DS-1","title":"A neutral base design system, themed by tokens, with Fieldnotes as one theme","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**A neutral base design system, themed by tokens, with Fieldnotes as one theme.** The platform draws every tenant with one neutral design system whose components read semantic tokens only. A tenant themes it by token values alone; Fieldnotes' editorial look becomes one theme among others, not the platform's look."},
    {"id":"d-ds-2","ref":"D-DS-2","title":"Tenants arrange their layouts, and a layout is data","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**Tenants arrange their layouts, and a layout is data.** A tenant arranges the regions and widgets of its screens. The arrangement is data the tenant edits, checked by the platform, never code."},
    {"id":"d-ds-3","ref":"D-DS-3","title":"Agentic first","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**Agentic first.** The platform is built to be composed by agents: an agent reads the backend specification and the frontend specification, composes the data and the screens a tenant asks for, configures them, and the tenant watches each step being applied live."},
    {"id":"d-ds-4","ref":"D-DS-4","title":"Wireframing is a first-class concept","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**Wireframing is a first-class concept.** An agent first produces a low-fidelity structural wireframe (regions, templates, pattern placeholders that will be bound to data, possibly before the data model exists), which renders at once, and refines it step by step to full fidelity. Each step is a valid state the tenant can see."},
    {"id":"d-ds-5","ref":"D-DS-5","title":"Public and private for every element, and nothing the data layer would refuse","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**Public and private for every element, and nothing the data layer would refuse.** Every element of the interface (an app, a page, a template region, a widget, a pattern instance, a field rendering, a navigation entry, a wireframe placeholder) is public or private to an audience, levels compose, and work in progress has its own audience. The interface never discloses what the data layer would refuse, including the existence of a hidden element, the label of a region left empty, counts and placeholders."},
    {"id":"d-ds-6","ref":"D-DS-6","title":"Role-based views","group":"Design system","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5457.","statement":"**Role-based views.** One page is seen by each person according to their roles: which widgets, regions, fields, actions and navigation entries appear, and whether an action is shown, disabled or hidden, follow the same policy and invoker evaluation the server uses, never a separate client rule. An admin control panel is seen by tenant admins only, by construction."},
    {"id":"d-ds-7","ref":"D-DS-7","title":"One machine-readable catalogue for tokens, themes, primitives, patterns, templates and display types (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**One machine-readable catalogue for tokens, themes, primitives, patterns, templates and display types.** specifications/ui-catalogue.jsonc lists every entry with a JSON Schema of its props, accepted examples and refused examples with their codes. specc generates the kernel's validator tables and the browser's interpreter tables from it, the gallery draws its examples, and the gateway serves it to agents; it carries a major.minor version, a composition records the major it was checked against, and the web application draws the current and the previous major through a tested migration."},
    {"id":"d-ds-8","ref":"D-DS-8","title":"Primitives are native elements with class contracts, and custom elements only for behaviour natives lack (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Primitives are native elements with class contracts, and custom elements only for behaviour natives lack.** A primitive with a native element (button, link, inputs, select, checkbox, radio, switch, progress) is that element with a ds-* class contract; a custom element is used only for dialog, menu, tabs, tooltip, toast region and the record picker, the last form-associated through ElementInternals. Every primitive renders into the light DOM. This makes D-FE-4 precise."},
    {"id":"d-ds-9","ref":"D-DS-9","title":"Display types are declared per object type, and the server resolves people and reference titles (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Display types are declared per object type, and the server resolves people and reference titles.** A presentation element per object type names its title field and a display type per field; a widget may override it. The gateway resolves principals to display names from the member directory and includes referenced records under the reader's policies. A field with no display type is drawn by a fallback of its type that never draws a record id, an epoch number or a JSON object."},
    {"id":"d-ds-10","ref":"D-DS-10","title":"Screens are compositions with drafts, and only a draft at full fidelity is published (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Screens are compositions with drafts, and only a draft at full fidelity is published.** A screen is a template, its regions and widgets, each widget a catalogue pattern bound to a section of the screen's view, a form, an action or a platform source, or a placeholder with a sample shape. The kernel checks every composition against the catalogue and the schema when it is defined. A screen holds a published body and, while it is built, a draft body that only builders are served; publishing is refused while the draft has a placeholder."},
    {"id":"d-ds-11","ref":"D-DS-11","title":"Visibility is declared and derived, and served per audience class by the server (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Visibility is declared and derived, and served per audience class by the server.** Every element declares an audience (public, members, or roles) no wider than its parent's; a widget, a column and an action also have a data audience the kernel derives from Read policies, role-only read rules and operation invokers. The gateway serves each audience class the manifest and parts filtered to what it sees, answers a part outside the class's manifest as an unknown part, sends only the anonymous class's parts as shareable, and keeps every other class's parts out of shared caches."},
    {"id":"d-ds-12","ref":"D-DS-12","title":"Roles vary one composition, and actions follow the kernel's preflight (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Roles vary one composition, and actions follow the kernel's preflight.** There is one composition per screen with audiences on its elements, never a copy per role. An action is absent when its operation's invokers exclude the viewer and, per row, allowed or refused by a kernel preflight of the invocation that the invocation itself runs. A screen must pass a content check: each least viewer of its declared audience sees at least one of its widgets. Builders preview a screen as a set of roles, with data limited to what both may read."},
    {"id":"d-ds-13","ref":"D-DS-13","title":"A tenant's layout is an overlay the tenant owns (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**A tenant's layout is an overlay the tenant owns.** The tenant's arrangement of a product's screen is a ui-layout element owned by the tenant, checked as the screen it leaves; an upgrade that removes something an overlay names is refused naming the overlay entries."},
    {"id":"d-ds-14","ref":"D-DS-14","title":"Agents build through product steps into the draft (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Agents build through product steps into the draft.** An agent writes a tenant app product and applies it in steps: a compile and a dry run, then an upgrade with the expected schema version into the draft, with a one-line label, each step at most 200 changes. Refusals are structured diagnostics with a code and a JSON Pointer into the product file. Risky data steps go through change proposals the owner approves; the owner publishes."},
    {"id":"d-ds-15","ref":"D-DS-15","title":"Themes are typed seeds and derived tokens, checked for contrast when defined, applied through the CSSOM (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Themes are typed seeds and derived tokens, checked for contrast when defined, applied through the CSSOM.** A preset gives every token; a tenant theme gives typed seeds and optional typed overrides from which the full set is derived. Defining a theme is refused when any pair the catalogue declares is below WCAG 2.2 AA in either scheme. Token values reach the page with style.setProperty after a type check, never as stylesheet text; fonts are the vendored families."},
    {"id":"d-ds-16","ref":"D-DS-16","title":"A product over the change cap is installed in stages (proposed)","group":"Design system","source":"Proposed in docs/design-system.md (WG-5457); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**A product over the change cap is installed in stages.** The installer splits a product of more than 200 changes into ordered stage versions, each at most 200 changes and each a complete installed version, applied as upgrades; the cap of one schema change and the all-or-none product change stay as they are."}
  ],
  "claims": [
    {"id":"ds-001","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the composition model, a composition that passes the composition check SHALL name only bindings the tenant schema defines.","rationale":"An agent's step is applied only after the check, so no state the tenant can see points at missing data.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::check_iff","lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::checked_bindings_resolve"],"ref":"DS-001","section":"Compositions and wireframes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Composition.check`","traces":["d-ds-10","d-ds-4","d-8250"]},
    {"id":"ds-002","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the composition model, a valid composition at full fidelity SHALL have every widget whose pattern needs data bound to a binding the tenant schema defines.","rationale":"Publishing requires full fidelity, so a published screen has no placeholder and no dangling binding.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::full_valid_bound"],"ref":"DS-002","section":"Compositions and wireframes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Composition.Full`","traces":["d-ds-10","d-ds-4"]},
    {"id":"ds-003","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the composition model, binding the placeholders of a valid composition one at a time to bindings the schema defines SHALL give a valid composition at every step and end at full fidelity.","rationale":"Refinement from wireframe to full fidelity is a sequence of valid states the tenant watches.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::bindAt_valid","lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::bindAt_unbound","lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::refine_valid","lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::refine_full"],"ref":"DS-003","section":"Compositions and wireframes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Composition.refine`","traces":["d-ds-4","d-ds-3"]},
    {"id":"ds-004","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the composition model, a schema change that removes no binding an unchanged screen names, with every changed screen passing the check against the new schema, SHALL leave every screen of the tenant valid.","rationale":"The kernel may check only the screens a change touches, plus the removal guard, and an upgrade cannot break a tenant overlay.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Composition.lean::incremental_valid"],"ref":"DS-004","section":"Compositions and wireframes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Composition.incremental_valid`","traces":["d-ds-10","d-ds-13","d-ds-14"]},
    {"id":"ds-005","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the theme model, the on-colour derived for a surface of any luminance SHALL meet the WCAG 2.2 AA contrast ratio for normal text against that surface.","rationale":"A theme derived from any accent a tenant picks has readable text on it, and the derivation's ramp search always ends.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Contrast.lean::onColour_meets_aa","lean/Strata/UI/Contrast.lean::search_finds"],"ref":"DS-005","section":"Tokens and themes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Contrast.onColour`","traces":["d-ds-15","d-ds-1"]},
    {"id":"ds-006","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the theme model, a theme that passes the theme check SHALL meet the WCAG 2.2 AA contrast ratio on every pair of tokens the catalogue declares.","rationale":"Contrast is a rule the tooling enforces when a theme is defined, not a review comment.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Contrast.lean::checkTheme_iff"],"ref":"DS-006","section":"Tokens and themes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Contrast.checkTheme`","traces":["d-ds-15","d-ds-1"]},
    {"id":"ds-007","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the visibility model, every element served to a viewer SHALL be in the viewer's declared and data audiences, under ancestors that are all in the viewer's audiences.","rationale":"The server decides what the browser is sent, so nothing the viewer may not see reaches the browser to be hidden there.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::render_sound"],"ref":"DS-007","section":"Visibility and roles","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Visibility.render`","traces":["d-ds-5","d-ds-11"]},
    {"id":"ds-008","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the visibility model, an element outside a viewer's audiences SHALL leave what the viewer is served unchanged wherever it sits among its siblings.","rationale":"The existence of a hidden widget, the label of a region it would fill and the number of hidden elements are not disclosed.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::hidden_leaves_no_trace"],"ref":"DS-008","section":"Visibility and roles","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Visibility.renderAll`","traces":["d-ds-5","d-ds-11"]},
    {"id":"ds-009","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the visibility model, the audience derived from an operation's invokers SHALL admit a viewer exactly when the kernel's invoke check does not refuse that viewer at its invoker stage.","rationale":"An action is shown from the server's own evaluation, so the interface and the invocation cannot disagree on who may act.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::audOf_sees"],"ref":"DS-009","section":"Visibility and roles","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Visibility.audOf`","traces":["d-ds-6","d-ds-12"]},
    {"id":"ds-010","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the visibility model, a signed-in viewer SHALL be in the data audience of an object type exactly when one of the viewer's roles has a Read grant on it.","rationale":"Role variation of data widgets is derived from the policies, not written beside them.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::dataAud_sees"],"ref":"DS-010","section":"Visibility and roles","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Visibility.dataAud`","traces":["d-ds-6","d-ds-11"]},
    {"id":"ds-011","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"design-system","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":7,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the visibility model, a screen that passes the content check SHALL show at least one of its widgets to every viewer it is served to.","rationale":"An admin panel whose widgets only an admin may read cannot be declared for every signed-in person, so a member is never served it with empty sections.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::content_check_nonempty","lean/Strata/UI/Visibility.lean::checked_screen_renders_content"],"ref":"DS-011","section":"Visibility and roles","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.UI.Visibility.contentCheck`","traces":["d-ds-6","d-ds-12"]}
  ]
}
